    "text": "To determine the combined weight of John, Mary, and Jamison, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine Mary's weight:**\n   Mary weighs 160 lbs.\n\n2. **Determine Jamison's weight:**\n   Mary weighs 20 lbs less than Jamison's weight.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Jamison's weight} = \\text{Mary's weight} + 20 = 160 + 20 = 180 \\text{ lbs}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine John's weight:**\n   John weighs one-quarter times more than what Mary weighs.\n   \\[\n   \\text{John's weight} = \\text{Mary's weight} + \\frac{1}{4} \\times \\text{Mary's weight} = 160 + \\frac{1}{4} \\times 160 = 160 + 40 = 200 \\text{ lbs}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the combined weight of the three:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Combined weight} = \\text{John's weight} + \\text{Mary's weight} + \\text{Jamison's weight} = 200 + 160 + 180 = 540 \\text{ lbs}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the combined weight of John, Mary, and Jamison is \\(\\boxed{540}\\).",
